 {:db/id "902c743a-020b-59b4-af9d-0ead240033fc"
  :question/id #uuid "902c743a-020b-59b4-af9d-0ead240033fc"
  :question/problem "**(a)** Show that $\\mathbf F$ has continuous first derivatives on and inside $C$ if and only if $\\mathbf G$ does."
  :question/answer-fields ["9247c709-6ec6-5fab-9361-a6bbbe35271d"]
  :question/worked-solution "Both fields use the same two scalar functions, with a sign change and a component swap. Check continuity of all four first partial derivatives on the same region; no application of Green's theorem is needed."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
 {:db/id "2a77ad0c-9822-5e2c-b80f-2602ffd6d7aa"
  :answer/id #uuid "2a77ad0c-9822-5e2c-b80f-2602ffd6d7aa"
  :answer/type :answer.type/text
  :answer/value "Using planar scalar curl,\n\n$$\\operatorname{div}\\mathbf F=f_x+g_y,\\qquad\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf G=f_x-(-g)_y=f_x+g_y.$$\n\nThe expressions are identical, so one is zero exactly when the other is zero. These are the definitions of source-free and irrotational, respectively."
  :db/ensure :answer/validate}
