 {:db/id "71c153c5-b242-591a-bc0e-031852d164f8"
  :answer/id #uuid "71c153c5-b242-591a-bc0e-031852d164f8"
  :answer/type :answer.type/text
  :answer/value "Potentials are $\\phi_F=(x^2-y^2)/2$ and $\\phi_G=xy$, since $\\nabla\\phi_F=(x,-y)$ and $\\nabla\\phi_G=(y,x)$. A stream function for $\\mathbf F$ is $\\psi=xy$.\n\nBoth curls are zero because the fields are gradients. Also, $\\operatorname{div}\\mathbf F=1-1=0$ and $\\operatorname{div}\\mathbf G=0+0=0$. Thus both have zero divergence and zero curl, as required here. Problem 1(b) gives $\\operatorname{div}\\mathbf F=\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf G=0$. Applying it to $\\mathbf G$, whose rotated field is $-\\mathbf F$, also gives $\\operatorname{div}\\mathbf G=-\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=0$. Problem 1(d) identifies the potential of $\\mathbf G$ with the stream function of $\\mathbf F$."
  :db/ensure :answer/validate}
 {:db/id "c479ba4b-591e-5cb9-a0e1-516fc2d62542"
  :answer-field/id #uuid "c479ba4b-591e-5cb9-a0e1-516fc2d62542"
