 {:db/id "a55585d2-0b0b-5446-a66e-5e37d60fbf20"
  :question/id #uuid "a55585d2-0b0b-5446-a66e-5e37d60fbf20"
  :question/problem "**(b)** $\\mathbf F=\\langle e^x\\cos y,-e^x\\sin y\\rangle$, $\\mathbf G=\\langle e^x\\sin y,e^x\\cos y\\rangle$ on $\\mathbb R^2$.\n\n(i) Confirm both are conservative. Use Problem 1 to show $\\mathbf F$ is an ideal flow (and so is $\\mathbf G$).\n\n(ii) Find potential functions for both fields. Use Problem 1 to derive a stream function for $\\mathbf F$."
  :question/answer-fields ["c5aecf12-592a-520d-8c44-f9e640f5c8e2"]
  :question/worked-solution "For the stream function, check $\\psi_y=e^x\\cos y=F_1$ and $\\psi_x=e^x\\sin y=-F_2$. When differentiating in $y$, the sign in $(\\cos y)'=-\\sin y$ matters. Potentials are defined on the entire stated plane."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
 {:db/id "2b0dd9f7-e858-58c2-9622-30b01c571ba7"
  :answer/id #uuid "2b0dd9f7-e858-58c2-9622-30b01c571ba7"
  :answer/type :answer.type/text
  :answer/value "The instruction that both fields are conservative is false on the full stated domain. A global potential for $\\mathbf F$ is\n\n$$\\phi_F=\\tfrac12\\ln(x^2+y^2)=\\ln r.$$\n\nHowever, $\\oint_{r=1}\\mathbf G\\cdot\\mathbf T\\,ds=2\\pi\\ne0$, so $\\mathbf G$ has no single-valued global potential on the punctured plane. Consequently $\\mathbf F$ has no single-valued global stream function there.\n\nLocally, after choosing a continuous angle branch $\\theta=\\arg(x+iy)$ on a cut domain, $\\nabla\\theta=\\mathbf G$. Thus $\\phi_G=\\theta$ and $\\psi_F=\\theta$ work locally; on $x>0$ one may use $\\theta=\\arctan(y/x)$.\n\nBoth fields nevertheless have zero divergence and zero curl at every point of the stated domain. With $s=x^2+y^2$,\n\n$$\\operatorname{div}\\mathbf F=\\frac{s-2x^2+s-2y^2}{s^2}=0,\\qquad\n\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\frac{-2xy+2xy}{s^2}=0,$$\n\n$$\\operatorname{div}\\mathbf G=\\frac{2xy-2xy}{s^2}=0,\\qquad\n\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf G=\\frac{s-2x^2+s-2y^2}{s^2}=0.$$\n\nSo both meet the worksheet's zero-divergence/zero-curl conditions without both being globally conservative."
  :db/ensure :answer/validate}
