 {:db/id "907e212d-1b2f-56e7-8af5-1ad42ba5d639"
  :question/id #uuid "907e212d-1b2f-56e7-8af5-1ad42ba5d639"
  :question/problem "**(c)** On $\\mathbb R^2\\setminus\\{(0,0)\\}$, let\n\n$$\\mathbf F=\\left\\langle\\frac{x}{x^2+y^2},\\frac{y}{x^2+y^2}\\right\\rangle,\\qquad\n\\mathbf G=\\left\\langle\\frac{-y}{x^2+y^2},\\frac{x}{x^2+y^2}\\right\\rangle.$$\n\n(i) Confirm both are conservative. Use Problem 1 to show $\\mathbf F$ is an ideal flow (and so is $\\mathbf G$).\n\n(ii) Find potential functions for both fields. Use Problem 1 to derive a stream function for $\\mathbf F$."
  :question/answer-fields ["9e1e9dba-f0f0-566b-bacd-0917f1f61821"]
  :question/worked-solution "Curl zero on a domain with a hole does not guarantee a global potential. Use Problem 2(b)'s nonzero circulation to disprove the global claim for $\\mathbf G$. A discontinuous principal angle or a multi-valued angle is not a single-valued differentiable potential on the whole punctured plane. Problem 1(d) transfers exactly this obstruction to a global stream function for $\\mathbf F$."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
