 {:db/id "2f3d1841-9934-5d9b-8ff9-00e6d5262f9c"
  :question/id #uuid "2f3d1841-9934-5d9b-8ff9-00e6d5262f9c"
  :question/problem "**(c)** Use (a) and (b) to prove the source's statement that “$\\psi$ is everywhere tangent to $\\mathbf F$.” That is, show that the **level curves** of a stream function are streamlines."
  :question/answer-fields ["39cb848b-3dc7-55a4-b390-6f24001982e0"]
  :question/worked-solution "It is the level curve, rather than the scalar function itself, that has a tangent. The slope proof needs $f\\ne0$; the gradient argument handles vertical tangents. A claim of a uniquely defined tangent at every critical point would need additional hypotheses, so retain the regular-point qualification."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
