  :multistep/id #uuid "df893de7-f13c-5602-9b56-5e571d7a8b23"
  :multistep/steps ["d985a7b6-8e60-5a31-bbae-2e977e7ef4d9" "2e731cbf-effb-54cf-ae8f-3968e42893e9" "5d6273ec-8db9-5610-a426-8e0e3a559bf4"]
  :multistep/first-step "d985a7b6-8e60-5a31-bbae-2e977e7ef4d9"
  :multistep/context "Source: Problem 5(a–c), PDF page 6.\n\n**Stream functions produce streamlines.** Let $\\mathbf F=\\langle f,g\\rangle$ be source-free and let $\\psi$ be its stream function, meaning\n\n$$\\psi_y=f,\\qquad\\psi_x=-g.$$\n\nLet $P=(x,y)$ lie on the level curve $\\psi(x,y)=c$. Think of the level curve locally as $y=y(x)$. The source's dependency diagram shows $\\psi$ depending on both $x$ and $y$, with $y$ itself depending on $x$; thus the composite is $\\psi(x,y(x))$."
