 {:db/id "805d0579-8e06-52e1-98ec-6d81588ca504"
  :question/id #uuid "805d0579-8e06-52e1-98ec-6d81588ca504"
  :question/problem "Source exercise: 3.1.9, printed page **127** (PDF page 139); the assignment sheet lists page 128.\n\nIdentify the operation that changes the first matrix to the second, and explain its effect on the determinant:\n\n$$\\begin{bmatrix}a&b\\\\c&d\\end{bmatrix}\\longrightarrow\\cdots\\longrightarrow\\begin{bmatrix}a&c\\\\b&d\\end{bmatrix}.$$"
  :question/answer-fields ["1b5e55df-c0dd-51ea-8df7-d165c685c016"]
  :question/worked-solution "The second matrix has the old rows as columns. Directly, the first determinant is $ad-bc$, and the second is $ad-cb=ad-bc$. This is transposition, rather than swapping two rows."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
