 {:db/id "1fb3669f-d6c2-5778-940b-a11e36dc9cd0"
  :question/id #uuid "1fb3669f-d6c2-5778-940b-a11e36dc9cd0"
  :question/problem "Source exercise: 3.1.24, printed page **129** (PDF page 141); the assignment sheet lists page 128.\n\nFind the determinant, **using row operations to simplify first**. Show your row operations and track their effects on the determinant.\n\n$$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1&2&1&2\\\\3&1&-2&3\\\\-1&0&3&1\\\\2&3&2&-2\\end{bmatrix}.$$\n\n$\\det(A)=$ {{answer}}."
  :question/answer-fields ["2b9aeba5-da06-5e9b-a4e0-532626735baf"]
  :question/worked-solution "First use $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-3R_1$, $R_3\\leftarrow R_3+R_1$, and $R_4\\leftarrow R_4-2R_1$. These row replacements preserve the determinant:\n\n$$\\begin{bmatrix}1&2&1&2\\\\0&-5&-5&-3\\\\0&2&4&3\\\\0&-1&0&-6\\end{bmatrix}.$$\n\nSwap $R_2$ and $R_4$ once, changing the determinant's sign. Then apply $R_3\\leftarrow R_3+2R_2$ and $R_4\\leftarrow R_4-5R_2$:\n\n$$\\begin{bmatrix}1&2&1&2\\\\0&-1&0&-6\\\\0&0&4&-9\\\\0&0&-5&27\\end{bmatrix}.$$\n\nFinally, $R_4\\leftarrow R_4+\\tfrac54R_3$ gives upper triangular diagonal entries $1,-1,4,63/4$. Its determinant is $-63$. There was one row swap, so $\\det(A)=63$."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
 {:db/id "a3033eeb-8f3e-53d2-b2aa-d827abb0de9b"
  :assigned-problem/id #uuid "a3033eeb-8f3e-53d2-b2aa-d827abb0de9b"
  :assigned-problem/content "1fb3669f-d6c2-5778-940b-a11e36dc9cd0"
  :assigned-problem/topic-coverage [[:topic/math-academy-id 1772] [:topic/math-academy-id 1773]]
