 {:db/id "aeff0721-b0ec-58e0-9819-86270bef6b68"
  :question/id #uuid "aeff0721-b0ec-58e0-9819-86270bef6b68"
  :question/problem "Source exercise: 4.2.3, printed page 151 (PDF page 163).\n\nDecide whether\n\n$$\\vec v=\\begin{bmatrix}4\\\\4\\\\-3\\end{bmatrix}$$\n\nis a linear combination of\n\n$$\\vec u_1=\\begin{bmatrix}3\\\\1\\\\-1\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\vec u_2=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\\\-2\\\\1\\end{bmatrix}.$$"
  :question/answer-fields ["fb07ab3d-0094-592c-9ddf-240db93273a6"]
  :question/worked-solution "Set $a\\vec u_1+b\\vec u_2=\\vec v$. The first two equations are $3a+2b=4$ and $a-2b=4$, giving $a=2$, $b=-1$. Check the third equation: $-a+b=-2-1=-3$. All three coordinates must agree."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
