 {:db/id "83017630-13a4-55f0-8afa-98393d3821c9"
  :question/id #uuid "83017630-13a4-55f0-8afa-98393d3821c9"
  :question/problem "Source exercise: 4.10.10, printed page 222 (PDF page 234).\n\nSuppose $\\{\\vec x_1,\\ldots,\\vec x_k\\}$ is a set of vectors in $\\mathbb R^n$. Show that $\\vec0$ is in $\\operatorname{span}\\{\\vec x_1,\\ldots,\\vec x_k\\}$."
  :question/answer-fields ["b78e587c-ee6e-563c-8b7d-dce6a4933d25"]
  :question/worked-solution "A span allows arbitrary real coefficients, including all zeros. The argument does not require the vectors to be nonzero or independent. Producing zero with all-zero coefficients does not demonstrate dependence; dependence requires a nontrivial zero combination."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
